1545
00:03:12,570 --> 00:03:13,880
Excuse m—

1546
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:14,860
My apologies.

1547
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:15,590
Oh, no…

1548
00:03:15,590 --> 00:03:17,460
Get to these documents without delay.

1549
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:18,590
Yes, sir.

1550
00:03:19,110 --> 00:03:21,100
This is from Lord Alexei.

1551
00:03:21,510 --> 00:03:24,680
Ah, thank you. Please take this to the office.

1552
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:25,620
Okay.

1553
00:03:25,620 --> 00:03:28,010
Excuse me, please take these too.

1554
00:03:28,010 --> 00:03:28,940
Sure.

1555
00:03:28,940 --> 00:03:29,860
And these as well.

1556
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:33,110
O-Okay…

1557
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:38,610
<i>Perhaps they should increase
the amount of workers here right now.</i>

1558
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:45,250
Lady Sharon, you came here
as a fiancée candidate for Lord Glen, right?

1559
00:03:45,250 --> 00:03:46,000
That's right.

1560
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:53,250
You will also be taking part in
the Holy Night's Banquet while in Sauslind, I presume?

1561
00:03:55,510 --> 00:03:58,380
Yes, though I will be doing one other thing while here.

1562
00:03:58,380 --> 00:04:03,770
I came here to do a little "insect repelling", if you will.

1563
00:04:04,370 --> 00:04:07,770
My sister Mireille will surely be overjoyed.

1564
00:04:08,610 --> 00:04:12,770
Lady Sharon, I feel we will become very good friends!

1565
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:21,740
<i>Lady Mireille… I'm also aware that the person
currently known as Lady Lamond was, a long time ago,</i>

1566
00:04:21,740 --> 00:04:24,290
<i>very close to being engaged to His Highness.</i>

1567
00:04:25,710 --> 00:04:28,790
I wonder why His Highness chose the Bibliophile Princess

1568
00:04:29,210 --> 00:04:31,540
over Miseral's Pearl Princess?

1569
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:35,990
I'm sure His Highness has his reasons.

1570
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:46,430
<i>At that time, I was under the impression that
I was a phony fiancée, so I answered unbothered. </i><i></i>

1571
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:48,810
<i>But now…</i>

1572
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:51,690
It's from Lady Mireille.

1573
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:58,840
Those look heavy. I'll help you, Lady Elianna.

1574
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:00,530
No, I've got it.

1575
00:05:00,530 --> 00:05:02,320
Don't be modest.

1576
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:04,200
It's okay.

1577
00:05:07,370 --> 00:05:11,620
What is it about my presence that goes unnoticed
even dressed as a professional?

1578
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:13,580
I am Alan.

1579
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:13,000
I am Alan...

1580
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:21,780
Oh dear, Lord Alan. Please accept my apologies.
I was just lost in my thoughts.

1581
00:05:24,980 --> 00:05:27,720
You said you were lost in thought.
Was it about Prince Chris?

1582
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:28,850
Well…

1583
00:05:28,850 --> 00:05:29,680
Hm?

1584
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:32,850
Please don't tell this to His Highness.

1585
00:05:33,950 --> 00:05:41,110
Hmm, what you don't want him to know about…
is it the annoying young noble lady?

1586
00:05:41,110 --> 00:05:43,580
Or maybe something else entirely?

1587
00:05:47,630 --> 00:05:48,790
Something else…

1588
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:54,150
Has Earl Dauner dug in his heels?

1589
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,380
Err…

1590
00:05:56,380 --> 00:05:58,970
Then it really is true.

1591
00:06:01,170 --> 00:06:06,220
<i>If my ideas are taken to enrich a country,</i>

1592
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:12,610
<i>I thought that I wouldn't mind if they spread
that idea and claimed it as their own.</i>

1593
00:06:14,010 --> 00:06:20,900
<i>However, if it's used by someone
who is a military diehard connected to Earl Dauner</i>

1594
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:30,580
<i>other countries may think that we are oriented
for military intervention conflict zone northeast of Sauslind.</i>

1595
00:06:31,030 --> 00:06:37,040
To think that I've interfered with His Highness' plans
with my careless remarks...

1596
00:06:39,250 --> 00:06:41,580
Oh, Lady Elianna.

1597
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:45,300
We're kinda focused on something else at the moment,
but don't worry about it.

1598
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:55,280
In my opinion, well, Prince Chris would never let you
be on the receiving end of all of that.

1599
00:06:56,360 --> 00:07:02,280
Then I'm just being protected by the prince,
like I always am.

1600
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:03,070
Huh?

1601
00:07:03,430 --> 00:07:06,230
You really are too serious for your own good.

1602
00:07:07,460 --> 00:07:11,370
Prince Chris' busyness right now is of his own making.

1603
00:07:11,370 --> 00:07:15,120
Go ahead and barge in on him,
that's nothing you need to worry about.

1604
00:07:17,210 --> 00:07:18,750
Okay.

1605
00:07:18,750 --> 00:07:23,760
Now then, I'm going to deliver these,
so go take those to Chris.

1606
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:28,720
Thank you, Lord Alan.

1607
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:35,980
<i>I've been so afraid of seeing His Highness
that I've avoided his office since morning.</i>

1608
00:07:37,030 --> 00:07:39,400
<i>I have to have a proper discussion with him.</i>

1609
00:07:44,790 --> 00:07:47,110
<i>He isn't here today either.</i>

1610
00:07:52,210 --> 00:07:56,660
She is of the same opinion, Prince Christopher.

1611
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:13,350
Preparations for the Holy Night's Banquet
are complete, but...

1612
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:18,060
you seem distracted, Lady Elianna.

1613
00:08:19,110 --> 00:08:21,020
My apologies.

1614
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:26,370
Are you concerned about the issue with the concubines
for His Highness that the queen hinted at?

1615
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:33,950
I do not believe the queen will speak of it,
so I will tell you.

1616
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:38,330
This reason Viscountess Dauner
is promoting her daughter, Lady Matilda,

1617
00:08:38,940 --> 00:08:43,540
is because she has entrusted her daughter
with her own unfulfilled dream, I believe.

1618
00:08:43,540 --> 00:08:44,460
Oh?

1619
00:08:44,740 --> 00:08:49,720
The Viscountess herself was a candidate
for marriage to His Highness in the past.

1620
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:56,680
So now, since your father, Marquess Bernstein,
is cutting the military budget every year,

1621
00:08:56,680 --> 00:09:03,040
he is not thought highly of
by those associated with the military.

1622
00:09:03,040 --> 00:09:06,360
In order to maintain balance in the inner court,

1623
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:12,360
it seems he's bringing his granddaughter into the court
as a concubine, to put pressure on the Prince.

1624
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:16,120
Now then, Lady Elianna, how will you proceed?

1625
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:18,330
What do you mean?

1626
00:09:18,330 --> 00:09:21,830
Historically, concubines have been essential
to the succession of monarchs.

1627
00:09:21,830 --> 00:09:26,340
Are you willing to accept the prince having concubines?

1628
00:09:26,340 --> 00:09:28,090
I...

1629
00:09:28,090 --> 00:09:30,880
And one more thing, Lady Elianna.

1630
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:33,590
About the leak of information,

1631
00:09:34,260 --> 00:09:37,190
is there a maid in the palace
that you suspect would do that?

1632
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:46,860
No. I can't imagine any of them would
do anything to betray the royal family.

1633
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:53,110
Lady Elianna, you have your own strengths.

1634
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:56,360
Please never forget that.

1635
00:09:57,400 --> 00:10:02,040
Now, moving on... I will tell you about
the guests for the Holy Night's Banquet.

1636
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:05,120
Okay.

1637
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:11,300
<i>In the end, I couldn't see His Highness yesterday either.</i>

1638
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:14,800
Morning, Sara.

1639
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:16,690
Good morning.

1640
00:10:19,140 --> 00:10:22,810
<i>I can't put this off any longer.</i>

1641
00:10:22,810 --> 00:10:28,280
<i>I must discuss my inappropriate comments
and the activity in the inner courts... ?</i>

1642
00:10:30,150 --> 00:10:32,320
<i>But, more importantly...</i>

1643
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:37,520
<i>I have to see His Highness
and have a proper talk with him.</i>

1644
00:10:44,730 --> 00:10:47,290
An accident at the Tessen River construction site?

1645
00:10:47,550 --> 00:10:51,480
A support beam for the bridge girder collapsed,
and some workers were injured.

1646
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:54,420
The site supervisor is young and inexperienced,

1647
00:10:54,420 --> 00:10:57,430
so perhaps they all lack the proper leadership.

1648
00:10:57,430 --> 00:11:01,430
I don't think so. He's from the Azul Region, after all.

1649
00:11:01,430 --> 00:11:05,440
The people respect him,
and he has a veteran advisor assisting him.

1650
00:11:05,950 --> 00:11:08,130
It's hard to imagine there'd be discord on the site.

1651
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:13,110
I should see the location myself.

1652
00:11:13,110 --> 00:11:17,320
Alec, adjust my schedule. Glen, prepare my horse.

1653
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:20,660
What?! Are you really going to the Azul Region right now?

1654
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:22,490
What about the Holy Night's Banquet?

1655
00:11:22,490 --> 00:11:24,620
I'll make it back in time for the banquet.

1656
00:11:24,620 --> 00:11:26,830
Now quit whining and get ready.

1657
00:11:26,830 --> 00:11:28,750
Yet another grueling, forced march...

1658
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:31,530
Your Highness, there's no reason for you to go yourself—

1659
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:35,630
Eli!

1660
00:11:38,010 --> 00:11:39,760
Y-Your Highness...

1661
00:11:40,250 --> 00:11:43,020
I need more of you, Eli.

1662
00:11:46,310 --> 00:11:50,670
Why do I see so little of you,
though we're in the same palace?

1663
00:11:50,670 --> 00:11:53,950
This must be deliberate, or some sort of conspiracy...

1664
00:11:53,950 --> 00:11:58,530
I was just about to have Glen teach me
how to steal into a woman's bedroom at night.

1665
00:11:58,530 --> 00:12:00,030
<i>Excuse me?!</i>

1666
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:02,610
Don't make me sound like a lecherous creep!

1667
00:12:02,610 --> 00:12:05,330
Any conspiracy would be traced back to you, Your—

1668
00:12:05,330 --> 00:12:10,330
What a bunch of unrefined louts they are,
interfering with a lover's rendezvous.

1669
00:12:10,970 --> 00:12:14,110
I’m sorry I haven’t had any time for you lately, Eli.

1670
00:12:14,110 --> 00:12:17,910
I'll be sure to make some time for you
by the new year holidays.

1671
00:12:22,810 --> 00:12:25,450
Okay, I understand.

1672
00:12:25,450 --> 00:12:26,200
Good.

1673
00:12:32,030 --> 00:12:34,110
U-Um...

1674
00:12:34,870 --> 00:12:36,790
Were you lonely, Eli?

1675
00:12:44,020 --> 00:12:46,660
If we're going, let's go, and let's get there fast.

1676
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:51,830
Right. Since you've got time to flirt,
you can get there fast and clear everything up.

1677
00:12:51,830 --> 00:12:53,130
Tch.

1678
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:59,510
There's an unseasonable amount of mosquitoes out now,
and I'm on extermination duty.

1679
00:12:59,870 --> 00:13:02,970
I have it under control, though, so don't worry.

1680
00:13:02,970 --> 00:13:09,140
Thank you, Your Highness.
Please be careful and return safely.

1681
00:13:09,140 --> 00:13:14,380
I will. I'm sorry to be in such a hurry, Eli,
but I'll be back soon.

1682
00:13:16,430 --> 00:13:19,150
<i>Though I was finally able to see His Highness,</i>

1683
00:13:19,150 --> 00:13:24,800
<i>my heart felt even heavier than before I met him. </i><i></i>

1684
00:13:26,950 --> 00:13:29,410
A few days later...

1685
00:13:26,950 --> 00:13:29,410
A few days later...

1686
00:13:26,950 --> 00:13:29,410
A few days later...

1687
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:32,420
Lady Elianna.

1688
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:35,480
Lady Sharon is waiting for you.

1689
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,420
She is?

1690
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:52,560
Lady Elianna, I'd like to have
a talk with you about something.

1691
00:13:53,530 --> 00:13:54,940
A talk?

1692
00:13:55,170 --> 00:13:58,840
Yes! Can the two of us speak?

1693
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:01,200
Lady Sharon.

1694
00:14:01,460 --> 00:14:03,450
You are excused as well, Elen.

1695
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:09,660
I hate beating around the bush, Lady Elianna.

1696
00:14:09,660 --> 00:14:10,640
All right...

1697
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:13,180
I'll get straight to the point, then.

1698
00:14:13,180 --> 00:14:18,090
I want to be Christopher's partner
for the Holy Night's Banquet instead of you.

1699
00:14:18,930 --> 00:14:20,040
Pardon me?

1700
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:24,090
If he attends the party with
someone from the Miseral Dukedom,

1701
00:14:24,450 --> 00:14:30,220
it will be clear to everyone else as well
that His Highness has a high regard for my big sister Mireille, right?

1702
00:14:31,290 --> 00:14:35,440
Also, considering how things will unfold
 I think it's the best course of action.

1703
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:37,980
How things will unfold?

1704
00:14:38,390 --> 00:14:42,230
I know that you will be the next queen...
the news has already spread.

1705
00:14:42,230 --> 00:14:49,990
Plus, Lady Mireille’s already been married once before—
though it was an official arrangement, nothing shady.

1706
00:14:49,990 --> 00:14:57,330
But if Lady Mireille were to marry Prince Christopher,
things would return to the way they should be.

1707
00:14:57,330 --> 00:15:00,880
You understand, don't you? They're the Yule Lovers.

1708
00:15:01,220 --> 00:15:03,110
The Yule Lovers?

1709
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:06,090
Jeez, you're just as slow as you look, huh?

1710
00:15:06,090 --> 00:15:09,760
It's the love story of Prince Christopher and Lady Mireille!

1711
00:15:10,490 --> 00:15:14,770
The princess and the prince from the neighboring country
loved each other since they were children!

1712
00:15:15,170 --> 00:15:21,350
Even though they made a promise for the future,
the prince has a fiancée thrust on him who gets in the way,

1713
00:15:21,350 --> 00:15:25,030
and the princess is forced to marry an old man.

1714
00:15:25,330 --> 00:15:28,280
Just when it looked like their relationship was doomed...

1715
00:15:29,530 --> 00:15:34,150
The princess is discovered to be the Yule maiden
who is loved by the goddess

1716
00:15:34,150 --> 00:15:36,540
and her purity was guarded
by the divine protection of the goddess.

1717
00:15:37,070 --> 00:15:40,170
Both the old man and the interfering fiancée are eliminated,

1718
00:15:40,520 --> 00:15:44,040
and the two live happily ever after!

1719
00:15:49,890 --> 00:15:56,310
In Miseral, everyone understands that the models for this book
are Prince Christopher and Lady Mireille.

1720
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,310
Oh, really?

1721
00:15:58,310 --> 00:16:00,810
That's why, Lady Elianna,

1722
00:16:01,140 --> 00:16:04,110
you ought to fix this broken relationship.

1723
00:16:04,110 --> 00:16:06,450
You're nothing but extra baggage to the prince.

1724
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:11,200
So I want you to release the prince.

1725
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:15,200
Release the prince, you say?

1726
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:17,830
Yes, if Lady Mireille were in your position,

1727
00:16:17,830 --> 00:16:23,460
she'd handle both the prince's concubines
and the nobles within the palace quite nicely.

1728
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:28,970
You can remain as a figurehead ruler
and continue to read your books all the time.

1729
00:16:28,970 --> 00:16:32,180
Lady Mireille will handle all the essential duties.

1730
00:16:32,970 --> 00:16:38,270
You understand, don't you? You're a nuisance in this story,

1731
00:16:38,270 --> 00:16:43,230
so vacate your position next to the prince
and let my big sister return to her rightful place.

1732
00:16:43,620 --> 00:16:48,110
That would be the most appropriate end for this tale.

1733
00:16:52,210 --> 00:16:53,910
<i>A nuisance...</i>

1734
00:16:58,660 --> 00:17:04,820
<i>I can't feel the murmur of the books that I always do...</i>

1735
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:10,760
<i>I don't know whether or not His Highness
is willing to take in concubines,</i>

1736
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:15,240
<i>and I won't know unless I ask him, but...</i>

1737
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:25,650
<i>What if I am in the way of Prince Christopher and Lady Mireille
loving each other since they were children?</i>

1738
00:17:28,270 --> 00:17:31,410
<i>I have to ask His Highness directly.</i>

1739
00:17:31,750 --> 00:17:36,910
<i>But then, what if he agrees?</i>

1740
00:17:38,690 --> 00:17:40,660
<i>I want to be with His Highness.</i>

1741
00:17:41,770 --> 00:17:50,840
<i>Since our feelings for each other were mutual,
I've tried my best to be worthy of being next to His Highness.</i>

1742
00:17:50,840 --> 00:17:52,110
<i>But...</i>

1743
00:18:00,060 --> 00:18:02,330
<i>I'm a little exhausted.</i>

1744
00:18:11,310 --> 00:18:12,820
I'll say it once more.

1745
00:18:14,570 --> 00:18:16,490
My brother...

1746
00:18:16,490 --> 00:18:19,080
Countess Anna Hayden...

1747
00:18:19,550 --> 00:18:24,080
will you attend the Holy Night's Banquet
with me as my partner?

1748
00:18:24,910 --> 00:18:26,710
Lord Alfred...

1749
00:18:26,710 --> 00:18:28,840
I'm being sincere, Lady Anna.

1750
00:18:29,550 --> 00:18:33,590
As a man, I am captivated by you.

1751
00:18:33,590 --> 00:18:36,600
Please, won't you be my partner?

1752
00:18:45,940 --> 00:18:47,740
It seems His Highness has returned.

1753
00:18:47,740 --> 00:18:49,900
I'm glad he's back in time for the banquet.

1754
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:51,110
Yes.

1755
00:18:54,660 --> 00:18:57,870
Come on, don't be so ridiculous, Prince Chris!

1756
00:18:58,370 --> 00:19:03,250
It's going to take time because
it's another country you're looking into.

1757
00:19:03,250 --> 00:19:07,750
If you have time for idle talk, then you've got time
to work with the intelligence department.

1758
00:19:08,050 --> 00:19:11,760
I'm making good use of the time I have
in between preparations for the Holy Night's Banquet,

1759
00:19:11,760 --> 00:19:14,550
so I hope you can tolerate me falling a little behind.

1760
00:19:14,550 --> 00:19:16,760
I may sue you for overwork.

1761
00:19:17,630 --> 00:19:23,020
Do it. It would all come back to me, anyways.
I'd crush you to a pulp.

1762
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:25,690
Yikes! What a tyrannical ruler!

1763
00:19:25,690 --> 00:19:28,650
Abuse of power, terrible working conditions
and regulations,

1764
00:19:28,650 --> 00:19:32,140
overthrowing a worker's basic human rights,
unfair overtime!

1765
00:19:32,140 --> 00:19:34,530
Prince Chris has donkey ears,
just like the king of legend.

1766
00:19:38,530 --> 00:19:40,760
Your Highness. Um...

1767
00:19:42,910 --> 00:19:47,010
I would like to postpone our wedding.

1768
00:19:59,470 --> 00:20:01,070
I'm sorry.

1769
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:33,670
Lady Elianna.

1770
00:20:34,670 --> 00:20:37,970
I saw you running by...

1771
00:20:40,230 --> 00:20:41,600
Oh, don't move.

1772
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:52,080
What mischievous holly,
to try to damage such lovely hair.

1773
00:20:57,450 --> 00:20:59,480
It's all right now.

1774
00:21:00,570 --> 00:21:01,560
Elianna.

1775
00:21:10,660 --> 00:21:12,880
Eli, let's talk this over.

1776
00:21:14,830 --> 00:21:19,130
Prince Christopher, you should cool your head a bit.

1777
00:21:19,130 --> 00:21:22,640
You have nothing to do with this. Stand back.

1778
00:21:22,640 --> 00:21:28,270
It's true I am not involved,
but I can't disregard a frightened woman.

1779
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:33,270
This problem is between me and her.
I'd appreciate it if you didn't interfere.

1780
00:21:33,270 --> 00:21:34,520
Come here, Eli.

1781
00:21:39,320 --> 00:21:45,660
I deeply apologize, Your Highness, but...
could you please give me some time?

1782
00:21:45,660 --> 00:21:48,770
I want to go home, just for today.

1783
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:55,000
All right. I get it....

